# Sprint Planner Workflow

Guide AI agents through structured ticket refinement, codebase research, planning, and parallel
execution for sprint work.

## Critical Workflow Rule

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ MANDATORY WORKFLOW - DO NOT SKIP PHASES                     │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                             │
│ 1. TRIAGE    → Read ticket, ask refinement questions        │
│ 2. RESEARCH  → Explore codebase, document findings          │
│ 3. PLAN      → Write step-by-step implementation plan       │
│ 4. APPROVE   → Present plan, wait for explicit approval     │
│ 5. EXECUTE   → Implement (parallel agents if applicable)    │
│ 6. COMPLETE  → Move ticket to completed/                    │
│                                                             │
│ NEVER skip to step 5. ALWAYS triage and research first.     │
│                                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Trigger Phrases

- "Refine this ticket"
- "Plan this ticket"
- "Let's work on [JIRA-ID]"
- "Research [JIRA-ID]"
- "Execute [JIRA-ID]"
- "Run tickets in parallel"
- "What's ready to execute?"

